## Q8 — Vector Products (4 marks)
**Spec ref**: F5
### Question
The vectors **a**, **b**, and **c** are such that:
$$\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}, \quad \mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$$
Work out (**a** − 4**b** + 3**c**) × (2**a**).
### Solution
Using properties of the cross product:
- **a** × **a** = **0** (any vector crossed with itself is zero)
- Cross product is anti-commutative: **b** × **a** = −(**a** × **b**)
- Cross product is distributive over addition
Expand:
$$(\mathbf{a} - 4\mathbf{b} + 3\mathbf{c}) \times (2\mathbf{a})$$
$$= 2(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{a}) - 8(\mathbf{b} \times \mathbf{a}) + 6(\mathbf{c} \times \mathbf{a})$$
$$= 2(\mathbf{0}) - 8(-\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) + 6(-\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c})$$
$$= 8(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{b}) - 6(\mathbf{a} \times \mathbf{c})$$
$$= 8\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} - 6\begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$$
$$= \begin{pmatrix} 16 \\ 8 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \\ 18 \end{pmatrix}$$
### Answer
$$\begin{pmatrix} 16 \\ 8 \\ -18 \end{pmatrix}$$
