$$\sum_{r=2}^{n} \frac{1}{(r-1)r(r+1)} > 0.249$$
[3 marks]
### Solution
**(a)**
Using partial fractions on 1/((r−1)r(r+1)):
$$\frac{1}{(r-1)r(r+1)} = \frac{A}{r-1} + \frac{B}{r} + \frac{C}{r+1}$$
1 = Ar(r+1) + B(r−1)(r+1) + C(r−1)r
Setting r = 0: 1 = A(0)(1) + B(−1)(1) + 0 → B = −1  
Setting r = 1: 1 = A(1)(2) + 0 + 0 → A = 1/2  
Setting r = −1: 1 = 0 + 0 + C(−2)(−1) → C = 1/2
So:
$$\frac{1}{(r-1)r(r+1)} = \frac{1}{2(r-1)} - \frac{1}{r} + \frac{1}{2(r+1)}$$
$$= \frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{1}{(r-1)} - \frac{2}{r} + \frac{1}{(r+1)}\right]$$
$$= \frac{1}{2}\left[\left(\frac{1}{r-1} - \frac{1}{r}\right) - \left(\frac{1}{r} - \frac{1}{r+1}\right)\right]$$
Let u(r) = 1/r − 1/(r+1) = 1/(r(r+1)). Then:
$$\frac{1}{(r-1)r(r+1)} = \frac{1}{2}[u(r-1) - u(r)]$$
where u(r) = 1/(r(r+1)).
By method of differences (telescoping):
$$\sum_{r=2}^{n} \frac{1}{(r-1)r(r+1)} = \frac{1}{2}\sum_{r=2}^{n}[u(r-1) - u(r)]$$
$$= \frac{1}{2}[u(1) - u(n)]$$
$$= \frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{1}{1 \cdot 2} - \frac{1}{n(n+1)}\right]$$
$$= \frac{1}{2}\left[\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{n(n+1)}\right]$$
$$= \frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{2n(n+1)} \quad \square$$
**(b)**
$$\frac{1}{4} - \frac{1}{2n(n+1)} > 0.249$$
$$\frac{1}{4} - 0.249 > \frac{1}{2n(n+1)}$$
$$0.001 > \frac{1}{2n(n+1)}$$
$$2n(n+1) > 1000$$
$$n(n+1) > 500$$
$$n^2 + n - 500 > 0$$
Testing: 22 × 23 = 506 > 500 ✓ and 21 × 22 = 462 < 500 ✗
### Answer (b)
**n = 22**
